{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ve reviewed your records from the outside hospital. You came in because of swelling and pain in your left ankle after a fall, and your INR was very high—12.3. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. I twisted it two weeks ago. It got worse, and I kept falling. The pain was unbearable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were on warfarin for blood clots, and your INR was too high, so you got vitamin K and FFP. We’ll monitor that closely. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still bad. I can’t put any weight on it. The boot helps, but I keep losing balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Ortho looked at your X-ray. No new fracture—just a severe sprain on top of an old avulsion injury. Surgery isn’t needed. Rest, elevation, and the boot are key."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I’m worried about falling again. I feel so weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get physical therapy to help with stability. For now, we’re holding warfarin and will restart it once your INR is safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my nausea? I’ve felt sick since I got here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed that. Your labs are mostly stable, but we’re checking your abdomen. You’ve had bowel issues before, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, fibrosing mesenteritis. I’ve had 23 surgeries. My stomach gets blocked sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2183-02-27 21:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re concerned you might be developing another partial blockage. We’ll do a CT scan tomorrow to check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT scan shows your stomach and duodenum are dilated—signs of a partial small bowel obstruction. It’s likely from adhesions, and possibly from the narcotics you’ve been taking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Does that mean surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Surgery isn’t recommended right now. We’ll manage it conservatively—NPO, IV fluids, and your G-tube will be used for suction to decompress your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no food at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for now. We’ll start TPN—nutrition through your port—to keep you nourished while your bowel rests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin? I’m scared of clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re bridging you with Lovenox until your INR is stable. We’ll restart warfarin at a higher dose later—7.5mg—because your levels have been hard to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I’ve been dizzy. Is that from the meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2183-02-28 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. You were a bit dehydrated and orthostatic. IV fluids should help. Your heart rate is high—around 106—but it’s likely from pain and deconditioning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2183-03-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures flagged coagulase-negative staph, but it’s likely a contaminant. You’ve had no fever since admission, so we’re stopping vancomycin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2183-03-01 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2183-03-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not in your case. It’s common with port access. We’ll keep it clean and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2183-03-02 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest KUB shows the obstruction is still there, but stable. We’re keeping the G-tube on suction. Any nausea today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2183-03-02 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little, but less than yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2183-03-02 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign. We’re continuing octreotide to reduce secretions. Once output drops, we’ll switch the G-tube to gravity drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2183-03-04 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CTA. No pulmonary embolism, but the images were limited. Your liver shows more fat than before, and you have portal hypertension signs. But no acute issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2183-03-04 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from my hepatitis C?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2183-03-04 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Fibrosing mesenteritis and repeated surgeries also contribute. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2183-03-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR dropped too low after vitamin K. We’ve restarted warfarin and are bridging with Lovenox until it climbs back to a safe range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2183-03-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be on Lovenox the whole time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2183-03-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just until your INR is therapeutic. Then we’ll stop it and continue warfarin at 7.5mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2183-03-06 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your TSH is elevated—5.6. Your levothyroxine dose was recently lowered, but now it seems too low. We’re increasing it to 88mcg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2183-03-06 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been tired. Could that be why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2183-03-06 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, fatigue is common with high TSH. This adjustment should help. We’ll check it again after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2183-03-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is stable at 10.5, even though you had a guaiac-positive stool. No active bleeding signs, so we’re not transfusing. Outpatient colonoscopy is recommended."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2183-03-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m always anemic. Is this worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2183-03-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s consistent with your baseline. We’re monitoring closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2183-03-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s X-ray shows the bowel obstruction is improving. Fewer air-fluid levels. We’re going to start advancing your diet slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2183-03-08 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have real food?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2183-03-08 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with clear liquids. If you tolerate it, we’ll move to soft foods. TPN will continue until you can eat enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2183-03-09 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You kept down apple juice and broth. Good job. We’re switching to full liquids today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2183-03-09 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so hungry. When can I eat solid food?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2183-03-09 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you do well today, we’ll try soft solids tomorrow. But go slow—your gut has been through a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2183-03-10 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now therapeutic. We’ve stopped Lovenox. You’re back on warfarin 7.5mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2183-03-10 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the bleeding risk?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2183-03-10 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve increased both warfarin and levothyroxine, which can raise bleeding risk. That’s why you must get your INR checked soon after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2183-03-11 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re tolerating soft foods well. We’re discontinuing TPN today. Your G-tube is now on gravity drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2183-03-11 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2183-03-11 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re working on it. PT says you’re safer with the walker. Once your pain is controlled and diet is stable, we’ll plan discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2183-03-13 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on a regular diet for two days with no nausea or pain. That’s excellent progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2183-03-13 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My ankle still hurts, but the boot helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2183-03-13 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a chronic injury. Keep using the boot, elevate it, and avoid falls. We’ll send instructions for home care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2183-03-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning discharge tomorrow. You’ll go home on octreotide injections, warfarin, and levothyroxine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2183-03-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2183-03-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Check your INR in a few days and see your PCP. Also schedule colonoscopy and thyroid follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2183-03-15 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final plan: Discharge tomorrow. You’re stable, eating well, and your labs are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2183-03-15 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was so worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2183-03-15 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Keep resting, take meds as directed, and call if you have swelling, severe pain, or bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2183-03-16 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Here’s your discharge summary. INR check in two days, and follow up with your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2183-03-16 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2183-03-16 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. You’re strong—you’ve been through a lot."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2183-02-27 21:28:00",
    "admission_end": "2183-03-17 12:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with fibrosing mesenteritis, multiple abdominal surgeries, and chronic pain, was admitted after a fall that worsened a chronic left ankle avulsion fracture. She presented with severe ankle pain, swelling, and a supratherapeutic INR of 12.3, requiring vitamin K and FFP. During admission, she developed a partial small bowel obstruction likely exacerbated by narcotic use, managed conservatively with NPO status, G-tube suction, TPN, and octreotide. Her INR initially dropped but was successfully re-anticoagulated with warfarin 7.5mg daily, bridged with Lovenox. Levothyroxine was increased to 88mcg due to elevated TSH. Anemia remained stable, and no active bleeding was confirmed. She improved with dietary advancement, discontinued TPN, and was discharged home ambulating with a CAM walker, on updated medication regimens with close outpatient follow-up for INR and thyroid function.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified fracture of ankle, closed",
      "Supratherapeutic INR",
      "Partial small bowel obstruction",
      "Fibrosing mesenteritis",
      "Anemia",
      "Tachycardia",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism"
    ]
  }
}
